<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sousse</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hadrumetum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sousse is a city on the eastern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a> as Hadrumetum and later the capital of the Roman province of Byzacena. Renamed Justinianopolis under Byzantine rule, it became an Aghlabid naval base after the Arab conquest, with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ribat">ribat</a> and a Great Mosque built in the 9th century. Its medina is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sousse.jpg" alt="Sousse" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mietek Ł · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tunezja,_Sousse_-_panoramio_(3).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
